& [InputContract] is strict and required
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-entry-stability/0.1
  + [reconciliation_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  + [pre_read] is one nonoptional WindowsSuppliedEntryAssemblyInput
  + [post_read] is one nonoptional WindowsSuppliedEntryAssemblyInput
  = must: deny unknown serialized fields, variants, omissions, and wrong types
  = must: call assemble_windows_supplied_entry_observation independently for pre_read before post_read
  - never: accept WindowsSuppliedEntryObservation directly as unvalidated input

& [NestedAssemblyContract] reuses current authority
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-entry-observation/0.1
  + [required_signature] is 4b2bf473-b10e-4ca6-a39b-f68c3a7f3719
  + [pre_read_fault] preserves side pre_read and exact nested assembly fault
  + [post_read_fault] preserves side post_read and exact nested assembly fault
  + [short_circuit] pre_read failure prevents post_read evaluation and every nested failure prevents comparison
  - never: conceal a nested assembly fault or release a partial pair

& [SyntaxIdentityContract] is equality and distinctness syntax only
  + [reconciliation_identity] must be nonzero
  + [entry_reference_identity] must be nonzero and equal between admitted observations
  + [pre_batch_identity] and [post_batch_identity] must be nonzero and distinct
  + [output] preserves every syntax identity exactly
  - never: interpret reconciliation identity as a session, clock, process, query, handle, object, path, or event identity
  - never: interpret pre_read and post_read names or distinct batch identities as proof of physical order or separate acquisition

& [ComparisonFieldContract] is a closed ordered vocabulary
  + [enum] is kind, policy_decision, reparse_tag, strong_identity, allocation_size, end_of_file, number_of_links, and supplied_stream_records
  + [order] is exactly the declaration order
  + [coverage] accounts for every admitted observation field except profile, batch identity, and entry-reference identity
  + [profile] is already fixed by nested assembly
  + [batch_identity] is governed by the distinctness gate
  + [entry_reference_identity] is governed by the equality gate
  - never: add, remove, reorder, alias, or weaken a compared field without source reprocessing

& [ExactComparisonContract] is deterministic
  + [kind] compares exact policy-decision kind
  + [policy_decision] compares the full decision including profile, kind, attributes, conditional case flags, component, and order key
  + [reparse_tag] compares exact u32
  + [strong_identity] compares exact volume serial and canonical file-ID text
  + [allocation_size] compares exact u64
  + [end_of_file] compares exact u64
  + [number_of_links] compares exact u32
  + [supplied_stream_records] compares exact vector length, order, names, sizes, allocation sizes, and source offsets
  + [difference] stops at the first field in canonical order whose values are not exactly equal
  - never: sort raw records, normalize text, tolerate a delta, compare a subset, or use weighted, lexical, probabilistic, or learned judgment

& [StablePairContract] is complete and inspectable
  + [profile] preserves the exact stability profile
  + [reconciliation_identity] preserves caller syntax
  + [entry_reference_identity] preserves the common token
  + [pre_batch_identity] and [post_batch_identity] preserve distinct tokens
  + [compared_fields] is exactly the fixed eight-value ordered field array
  + [pre_read] preserves the exact admitted pre-read observation
  + [post_read] preserves the exact admitted post-read observation
  + [release] occurs only after every nested, syntax, and comparison gate passes
  - never: collapse the pair into a boolean or a single observation
  - never: construct TopologyEntryObservation, TopologyReceipt, or admission output

& [FaultContract] is closed and bounded
  + [codes] are profile, reconciliation_identity, pre_read, post_read, entry_reference, batch_identity, difference, resource, and json
  + [nested_side] is absent except for pre_read and post_read faults
  + [nested_fault] is absent except for pre_read and post_read faults and preserves the exact existing assembly fault
  + [difference_field] is absent except for difference and then contains exactly one StabilityComparedField
  + [field] is deterministic
  + [message] is limited to 256 Unicode scalar values
  - never: release a stable pair together with a fault
  - never: place unbounded nested JSON or observation values in a diagnostic

& [SemanticStrengthContract] prevents provenance inflation
  + [pre_read] is a caller-designated role
  + [post_read] is a caller-designated role
  + [stable] is exact equality under this supplied-value profile
  + [difference] is disagreement between admitted supplied values
  + [reconciliation] is comparison and accounting only
  - never: claim physical before or after ordering
  - never: claim same handle, object, query, buffer, thread, process, path, filesystem, or Windows origin
  - never: claim freshness, query completion, initialized buffers, physical stream completeness, content stability, supported platform, trust, or absence of change

& [DataDesignContract] is explicit
  + [conceptual_model] compare two caller-designated entry-local observations for closed supplied equality
  + [logical_model] strict request to nested assembly to syntax gates to canonical comparison to pair or fault
  + [physical_model] safe deterministic in-memory Rust values and strict serde
  + [identity_namespace] caller-owned and limited to one invocation
  + [source_data] two AssemblyInput values
  + [derived_projection] StablePair or ReconciliationFault
  + [state] absent
  + [persistence] absent

& [ImplementationBoundary] is zero effect
  + [authorized_file] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_entry_stability.rs
  + [authorized_export] is one exact library-module export
  + [authorized_tests] are module unit tests, one independent static surface test, one evidence rehash test, and workspace regression tests
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero
  + [lockfile_delta] is zero
  + [unsafe] is denied
  + [production_imports] are std, serde, and windows_supplied_entry_observation
  - never: use windows-sys, filesystem, process, environment, clock, random, network, model, persistence, handle, pointer, buffer, physical query, content read, path, traversal, Git, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, review execution, cleanup, or promotion APIs

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-ESR-001 through M2B-ESR-012
  + [requirements] are strict outer input, independent nested assembly, reconciliation identity, entry-reference equality, batch distinctness, exact comparison, first-difference classification, atomic release, full preservation, strict serialization, provenance nonclaims, and zero-effect proof closure

& [AcceptanceContract] is exact
  + [source] manifest matches exact SHA-256 and byte count
  + [authority] governing signature binds every processed SJS stage and current prerequisite signature
  + [focused] module unit tests and one independent static test pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [behavior] every requirement, comparison field, syntax gate, nested side, and failure mode has a direct test or static proof edge
  + [effects] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, unsafe, platform, and runtime-effect deltas remain zero
  + [evidence] clone-portable manifest hashes canonical, module, tests, solution, proof, review, and narrative
  + [global] workspace debug and release tests, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and audit pass
  + [downstream_gate] physical producer, content read, traversal, fixture, receipt, and admission remain absent

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure implementation only
  + [allowed] one deterministic in-memory module, export, serialization, focused tests, static test, evidence support, solution, proof, review, and governed narrative
  + [forbidden] Win32, windows-sys, unsafe, handles, pointers, buffers, filesystem, process, environment, clock, network, persistence, models, paths, content reads, physical fixtures, query execution, traversal, Git, receipts, admission, mutation, seal, review execution, cleanup, or promotion

